course: dictionary
lesson: 1029
title: Bookshelf: furniture for books
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A bookshelf is a shelf, or a piece of furniture with several shelves, for keeping books. Its plural is bookshelves: one bookshelf, two bookshelves. The word is made from two smaller words, book and shelf, joined together.
explain: «A tall bookshelf or chest of drawers can tip over when a child climbs it or pulls out its drawers, which is why grown-ups fix tall furniture to the wall.» The sentence tells you a bookshelf is tall furniture. It can be dangerous if a child climbs it, so grown-ups fix it to the wall. Chest of drawers is another piece of furniture, a clue that bookshelf is one too.
explain: «Inside: little sleeping bunks, a little table that folded up against the wall, a cooking-stove, lockers, bookshelves…» Bookshelves sits in a list with bunks, a table and a cooking-stove. Those are things you find in a home, so bookshelves are things you put books on, not things you read.
fact: A bookshelf is a shelf, or a piece of furniture with several shelves, for keeping books.
fact: The plural of bookshelf is bookshelves.
fact: A bookshelf is also called a bookcase.
fact: Tall bookshelves can tip over, so grown-ups fix them to the wall to keep children safe.
fact: Bookshelf is a compound word: book and shelf joined together to make one new word.
exercise: «Books were kept on the tall bookshelf in the classroom.» What is a bookshelf? | A small table for eating lunch | A bag for carrying books to school | *A shelf, or furniture with several shelves, for keeping books
exercise: What is the plural of bookshelf? | bookshelfes | *bookshelves | bookshelfs
exercise: The word bookshelf is made from two smaller words. Which two? | *book and shelf | paper and shelf | book and page
test: «A tall bookshelf can tip over when a child climbs it.» Why do grown-ups fix tall furniture to the wall? | To make the room look bigger | To make it easier to paint the walls | *To keep children safe from falling furniture
test: In the list «bunks, a table, a cooking-stove, lockers, bookshelves», what kind of word is bookshelves? | A verb, an action word | An adjective, a describing word | *A noun, a naming word for a thing
exam: What is a bookshelf, and what is its plural? | A kind of bookmark; plural bookmarks | *A shelf, or furniture with several shelves, for books; plural bookshelves | A page of a book you have finished; plural bookpages
